READLINK(1)                 User Commands

NAME
    readlink - print the target of a symbolic link

SYNOPSIS
    readlink [-fn] file...

DESCRIPTION
    readlink prints the target stored in each symbolic link, one per
    line, exactly as ln -s stored it. With -f it prints instead the
    absolute path of each file with every symbolic link and every . and
    .. resolved, and a file that is not a link is accepted. -n omits the
    newline after each name.

    The exit status is 1 when a file is not a symbolic link, does not
    exist, or cannot be resolved because it passes through more than 40
    links.

EXAMPLES
    readlink /etc/tests/link-motd
    readlink -f ../lib

SEE ALSO
    ln(1), ls(1), stat(1)
